rent workspace.ts function:\n- GET only - returns `{ workspace: { id, name } }`\n- No support for PUT/PATCH to update workspace settings\n\n### 7. **Key Implementation Patterns**\n\n**Page Pattern** (e.g., Members.tsx, Teams.tsx, Labels.tsx):\n```typescript\n- useEffect with dispatch(fetchXXX()) on token change\n- Redux selectors for data, loading, error states\n- Modal/inline edit patterns\n- Success/error handling with async dispatch\n- Page structure: header with title + action button, then list/grid\n```\n\n**Component CSS Pattern**:\n- Each component has `.tsx` and `.css` pair\n- Consistent class naming: `.component-name`, `.component-section`, etc.\n- Uses CSS variables for theming\n- Responsive with media queries (640px breakpoint)\n\n**Form Pattern** (TeamSettings.tsx as reference):\n- Inline editing with ref.focus() and .select()\n- Validation with error state\n- Confirmation dialogs for destructive actions\n- Success feedback (though may be missing for some actions)\n\n### 8. **Settings Implementation Status**\n\n**What Exists:**\n- Sidebar routing to `/settings` ✓\n- workspace.ts can fetch workspace ✓\n- workspaceSlice can fetch workspace ✓\n\n**What's Missing:**\n1. `Settings.tsx` page component\n2. `WorkspaceSettings.tsx` component\n3. `workspaceSlice.ts` needs:\n   - `updateWorkspace` async thunk\n   - State for `defaultTeamId`\n   - Handling default team persistence\n4. `workspace.ts` netlify function needs:\n   - PUT/PATCH endpoint to update workspace name and default team\n5. `Settings.css` stylesheet\n6. Integration with team selector in CreateIssueForm\n\n---\n\n## Summary for Implementation\n\nTo implement the Settings page with WorkspaceSettings component:\n\n1. **Create `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/pages/Settings.tsx`** - Main page wrapper\n2. **Create `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/WorkspaceSettings.tsx`** - Form component\n3. **Create `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/WorkspaceSettings.css`** - Styling\n4. **Update `workspaceSlice